From 7c7b47e1562d00044eb8c646f2fd0df98e3a0cc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:24:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: q3_0 K/V cache type (3.5 bpw)

Block of 32: f16 delta d, then 8 bytes of 2-bit low parts and 4 bytes of 1-bit high parts; x = d * (q - 4), q in
0..7. CPU and CUDA quantize and dequantize, copy into the K/V cache, flash-attention vec and MMA instances,
--cache-type-k/-v q3_0.

Measured on 6a4851286 (the same change on 2cadbfb64), RTX 2060 SUPER 8 GB launcher: perplexity +0.03 % at 64k vs
q4_0, 1.31x positions in VRAM, decode +23 % at 128k and +15 % at 192k, needles 12/12 and copies 10/10 at 160k,
HumanEval 160/164 (issue #21: P108, P114, P117).
